
AMISOR borehole AM06 MICROCAT data for 2012/2013 season
-------------------------------------------------------

Data from the first download.

ascii format
------------
contained in column formatted files catxxxx_3.dat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. The columns are:

1. decimal time - decimal days, where 0.0 = 0000 on January 1st 2001.
So, for example, midday on 15th January 2001 is decimal time 14.5
2. temperature (deg. C, T90)
3. conductivity (mS/cm)
4. pressure (dbar)
5. salinity (PSS78)
6. to 11. day, month, year, hour, minute, second.

* Note that all times are UTC.

* There is a line of data for each recording interval (i.e. no gaps),
and null data is represented by -999.0

* Clock errors were small (< 20 seconds), and no clock drift corrections have 
been made.

* Mean pressures over this latest download:

cat7325 =  bad pressure sensor: p=551.3 dbar used for whole time series
cat7324 =  679.5 dbar
cat7323 =  790.0 dbar


* Original pressure data for microcat 7325 are bad, and all conductivity and
salinity data were recalculated with the single pressure value of 551.3 dbar
i.e. the pressure immediately after deployment in January 2010.
Note that for previous season's data for this microcat, in hindsight
it is obvious that pressure data are bad, and for 2011/12 data the files that should be used
are cat7325_2meanp.dat and cat7325_2meanp.mat (i.e. with data
recalculated using the single pressure value of 551.3 dbar).



matlab
------
contained in matlab format files catxxxx_3.mat, where
xxxx = microcat serial number. 



